preConditionHook:
// Brooks's barbwire, mechanized per R22-03: how much of the MIDDLE bar of the
// last three lies inside the block its two neighbours span, plus a doji
// somewhere in the three.
//
// EL, written lowercase as the feature register does (EasyLanguage is
// case-insensitive): minlist(high[1], maxlist(high, high[2])) - maxlist(low[1],
// minlist(low, low[2])). maxlist/minlist are ACCEPTED in EL_FEATURES only for selection
// among tick-grid PRICE operands, which is exactly this case -- the operands
// are raw highs and lows, so any two of them are equal or differ by at least a
// tick, 1e9-1e11x the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance. Whether maxlist carries
// that tolerance therefore cannot change the selection, and the plain C++
// comparisons below stand in for it. Every scratch value is a declared local,
// not a hook-scope declaration, so a second placement of this rule gets its
// own prefixed copy.
//
// No clamp on a non-overlapping middle bar: middleOverlap simply goes negative
// and the condition's right-hand side is never negative, so the test fails --
// the same outcome BarOverlapFraction reaches with an explicit clamp, and the
// EasyLanguage twin is the unclamped expression.
nbHigh = high[2];
if (high[0] > nbHigh) nbHigh = high[0];
nbLow = low[2];
if (low[0] < nbLow) nbLow = low[0];
topEdge = high[1];
if (nbHigh < topEdge) topEdge = nbHigh;
botEdge = low[1];
if (nbLow > botEdge) botEdge = nbLow;
middleOverlap = topEdge - botEdge;
// EL: countif(absvalue(close - open) <= dojiBodyFraction * (high - low), 3).
// countif counts bars 0..N-1 INCLUDING the current bar and the counted
// condition is a true series, so bar i tests its own body against its own
// range (EL_FEATURES `countif`, VERIFIED). The counted condition is on prices,
// which have real history, so no zero-filled variable mirror is needed. The
// window is 3 because barbwire is a three-bar pattern -- structural, not
// tunable. dojiBodyFraction's 0.2 default matches the merged DojiBar rule so
// the corpus agrees on what a doji is.
dojiCount = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
    if (el_le(std::fabs(close[i] - open[i]), dojiBodyFraction * (high[i] - low[i]))) {
        dojiCount += 1;
    }
}
